-- title:
--   Inertia-fixed node presentation xy=q^eu at supersingular places
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a level $N\ge 1$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$, together with modular polynomial data `data` for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence `hKr` (reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $q$ equals $(Y^{q}-X)(Y-X^{q})$), the integrality hypotheses `hα`, `hβ` for the two degeneracy maps at level $N$ and prime $q$, a place specialisation $P$ of the modular curve of level $N$ at $A$ relative to these data, and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$. Assume $q\nmid N$; that $\mathrm{red}$ has kernel the maximal ideal of $A$; that $R$ is a model (the two divisor laws and the two cusp laws) and satisfies the fixed-place order law `OrderLawFixed`; and that $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC k N`, each rational, affine for $j$ and $j_N$ and with supersingular $j$-value, for which $R$ satisfies the regularity law and the node value law. Let $w\in W$. Then there is a number field $K_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, fixed pointwise by the inertia subgroup `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, such that on the coefficient subring $A\cap K_0$ the reduction `NodeLocalized.redRestrict red K₀` vanishes exactly on the multiples of $q$, and there exist node coordinates $c$ of $R$ over $K_0$ at $w$ — elements $x,y$ of the node ring `R.nodeIntegersOver K₀ w` with first residue of $x$ zero, order $1$ of the second residue of $x$ at the Frobenius translate of $w$, second residue of $y$ zero and order $1$ of the first residue of $y$ at $w$ — and a unit $u$ of that ring with $x\,y = (\text{constant }q)^{e}\,u$, where $e$ is `placeWidthChar q N w`. Moreover the ideal generated by the constant $q$, $x$ and $y$ is maximal and is the only maximal ideal of `R.nodeIntegersOver K₀ w`; the ideals generated by $(q,x)$ and by $(q,y)$ are prime with $y$ outside the first and $x$ outside the second; the node ring is Noetherian; and every element $g$ of it differs from the constant attached to some element of $A\cap K_0$ by a non-unit.
--
--   This is the level-$N$ presentation of a supersingular crossing on the special fibre: the local ring of the model of $X_0(Nq)$ at the node over $w$ is local, Noetherian, with residue field generated by constants, and its two branches cross with $xy$ equal to $q$ raised to the width of the node times a unit, all over a base field unramified at $q$ and fixed by inertia. It is used in the construction of the annulus data attached to supersingular places and in the analysis of the component group.
